{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Software Requirements!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe software requirements."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about software requirement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you are creating your own company, think about what types of software requirements will you need."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In which areas would you like to implement software?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write your ideas about these questions and share them with your instructor. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collect information and read about the topic. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about useful software in my own company. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I tell to my instructor about my work. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions with the Simple Present and Questions with the Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use different grammar structures when asking <span class=\"strong\">questions</span> in the <span class=\"strong\">simple present tense</span> and in the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous tense.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present Tense Interrogative Form</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous Tense Interrogative Form</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you need to ask a yes/no question, you use this structure:<br /> <br />  <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Auxiliary verb <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Do/ Does</span> + subject + Main verb in base form + complement + ?</div><br /><br />  Example:<br /> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Do</span> you need a new software system? <br /> Yes, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">do</span>. / Yes, I need a new software system.<br /> No, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">don't</span>. / No, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">don't</span> need a new software system.</span><br /><br />   As you can see, regarding short answers, you use the same auxiliary verb (do/does).<br /><br />  On the other hand, when you need to ask an information question (Wh- question), you use this structure:<br /><br />   <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Wh-question</span> + auxiliary verb <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Do/ Does</span> + subject + Main verb in base form + complement + ?</div><br /><br />  Example:<br /> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Why do</span> you need a new software system? <br />Because I need to gather my clients' information in a better way.</span><br /><br />In this case, your answer can't be short since you need to give information about it. So you never answer with the auxiliary verb (do/does).\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you need to ask a yes/no question, you use this structure:<br /><br />  <div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Auxiliary verb <span class=\\\"strong\\\">To be</span> + subject + Main verb + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> + complement + ?</div><br /><br />  Example:<br /> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Are</span> you sort<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> the requirements now?<br /> Yes, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">am</span>. / Yes, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">am</span> sort<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> the requirements now.<br /> No, I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m</span> not. / No, I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m</span> not sort<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> the requirements now.</span><br /><br />  As you can see, regarding short answers, you use the auxiliary verb to be.<br /><br />  On the other hand, when you need to ask an information question (Wh- question), you use this structure:<br /><br />   <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Wh-question</span> + auxiliary verb <span class=\\\"italic\\\">To be</span> + subject + Main verb + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">ing</span> + complement + ?</div><br /><br />    Example:<br />  <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> What </span> type of requirements <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are</span>  you sort<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span>?<br />I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">am</span> sort<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> functional and non-functional requirements.</span><br /><br />In this case, your answer can't be short since you need to give information about it. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What are you doing?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Why do they tangle?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Why does eco-bikes need a software?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What requirements are they demanding?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressions Related to Software"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Expressions are phrases we frequently use in our daily life."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When talking about software and computing, we can find several expressions that are commonly used in these fields. Learning expressions of that type help us to understand and communicate better with our coworkers.<br /><br />  In the chart below there are some common expressions you need to learn if you work with software and computing."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Expression</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Back up your files </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To make a support copy of your information.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Run out of room</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you don't have more space left. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Put your backups in a safe place</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Store your support copies where you won't miss them.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Hack into the network</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To enter the network with no allowance. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Wipe out the information</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To clean your storage device by erasing information.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm making a back-up of the software requirement files for the eco-bikes company."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't want my computer to wipe out that extremely important information."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tangle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complicate  something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't understand why companies tangle in those complicated software systems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "burden"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pressure someone to do more than he or she can do"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The idea is not to burden workers unnecessarily but to diminish their time for performance. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "well-known"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "famous, popular"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They want to create a network of eco-bikers in the country to become well-known."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feasible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something is possible to achieve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I need to collect, analyze, and document the clients' requirements to make sure the project is feasible. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "demanding"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "rigorous, hard"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As you can see, their functional requirements are very demanding."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "income"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the money the company earns "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to implement a software system to improve customer service and increase their income."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le01ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Molly: </span> Hi, Tom! What are you doing? </br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Tom: </span> Hi, Molly! I'm backing up the software requirement files for the eco-bikes company. I don't want my computer to wipe out that extremely important information.  </br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Molly: </span> I don't understand why companies tangle in those complicated software systems. </br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Tom: </span> Why do they tangle? Well, software systems facilitate the mission of the companies, that's why companies invest in software design. The idea is not to burden workers unnecessarily but to diminish their time for performance. And, in the same way, to improve customer service and increase their income.</br>"}, {"time": "37000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Molly: </span> Why does eco-bikes need a software?</br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Tom: </span> They need a software to track bicycles in case they are stolen, and also to store routes that the bike users discover. They want to create a network of eco-bikers in the country to become well-known, so they establish the company as a major bike provider. </br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Molly: </span>And, what are you doing for the eco-bikes project now? </br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Tom: </span> Well, as I'm the analyst, I have to describe the features and functionalities of the target system, more specifically the requirements for the eco-bikes system. Also, I need to collect, analyze, and document the clients' requirements to make sure the project is feasible."}, {"time": "78000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Molly: </span> What requirements are they demanding? </br>\n<span class =\"strong\">Tom: </span> There are several types of requirements, as in every project. For example, they have special design requirements. The system has to be easy to use so users like it. They have lots of customer requirements because the software has to be consistent with the vision of the company; that is to say, to generate environmentally friendly products.  There are lots of facilities they want to include in the software; some of them include chat, maps, route planning, and timing. As you can see, their functional requirements are very demanding."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le01ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about software requirement at a specific place."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain why software is required by a company."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give examples of software requirements."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think companies invest in software design?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think are the most common software